cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Pike Place Market — the twelve acres, counted"
message: "If you use the tenure figures or the inside-and-outside comparison, please cite this."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "NaNoBotCo"
    website: "https://nanobotco.github.io/"
url: "https://nanobotco.github.io/pike-place-market/"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A directory and GIS map of the Pike Place Market Historical District, Seattle,
  bounded by the district's own polygon (Seattle Land Use Code chapter 25.24, overlay
  PP). Every active city business licence on the district's streets is placed against
  the city's Master Address File and tested against that polygon, giving a dated,
  address-level record of who trades inside the line. Includes a comparison of licence
  tenure inside the district against licensed businesses within 150 m of it and outside,
  and a reconciliation of five separate counts of the same place. Building outlines,
  paths and points of interest are ODbL 1.0, © OpenStreetMap contributors.
keywords:
  - Pike Place Market
  - Seattle
  - historic district
  - business licences
  - GIS
  - OpenStreetMap
  - open data
  - vendor directory
